 "drivingQuestion": "Whose limits govern water drawn from a public cistern for someone else?",
 "outcome": "inconclusive",
 "outcomeNote": "Dispute recorded without decision in this unit.",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "beitzah.39a.14",
   "daf": "39a",
   "sentenceId": 13,
   "he": "וְשֶׁל עוֹלֵי בָבֶל — כְּרַגְלֵי הַמְמַלֵּא. אִתְּמַר: מִילֵּא וְנָתַן לַחֲבֵירוֹ, רַב נַחְמָן אָמַר: כְּרַגְלֵי מִי שֶׁנִּתְמַלְּאוּ לוֹ, רַב שֵׁשֶׁת אָמַר: כְּרַגְלֵי הַמְמַלֵּא.",
   "en": "§ The mishna states: «And» water drawn from a cistern «of those who come up» to Eretz Yisrael «from Babylonia,» i.e., a public cistern, is «as the feet of whoever fills» his vessel with its water. «It was stated» that amora’im disagreed with regard to this issue: In the case of one who «filled» a vessel with water from a public cistern on behalf of «another and gave» the water «to» him, «Rav Naḥman said:» The water is «as the feet of the one for whom they were filled; Rav Sheshet said:» It is «as the feet of the one who filled» it."
  }
 ],
